  "requirement": "Marks an agent request that can still accept reusable context before adding node contents.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct ContextPhase;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject, `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.ContextPhase`, declares a public marker type, `pub struct ContextPhase;`. It describes the type as the state of an agent request that can still accept reusable context. Its only testable obligation is that this public unit struct exists in the SDK at the specified path and item kind.\n\n`crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` covers that obligation. The requirement declaration points at it with a `:test:` anchor. The test runs `cargo doc` for the crate and builds the documented export inventory from the generated rustdoc. It compares that inventory with the inventory specified in `md/requirements/sdk`, then asserts that nothing is missing or unexpected. Removing `ContextPhase`, making it private, or changing it from a struct would make the assertion fail. The implementation is `struct[ContextPhase]` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs`, marked `{impl}` for `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.phases`.\n\nThe text imposes no other obligation on the type. The behaviour that the context phase accepts context (`Ask<…, ContextPhase>::context`) belongs to `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.agent_context` and the phase-transition requirements. Those are cited or implemented separately and are not reassessed here. The marker has no conditionals or transformations of its own, so no further test is needed.\n\nI found no gaps and no acknowledgments are needed.",
